ts to the fact  that there are minority Rhian groups who  completely disagree with everything that  is being shown in mainstream culture and  who are holding their own these poets  and their their artist and activist  friends are collaborating with  communicating with and standing with  their counterparts in Ukraine in Poland  and have a great deal more in common  with American language poets and  activists and then people might think do  these poets correspond what you each  other or meet with each other  is there any do they have any kind of  relationship or very much so this is  this is one of the ways that I've  delimited my project why I'm trying to  think of it again as a as a loose  constellation these poets all published  in the journal Tehran states which has  been the absolute heart of my project  but then they've also collaborated with  each other in readings sometimes staging  dramas and in a chat book series the  craft series and then with translations  and original texts in the free marxist  press they're constantly coming up with  new projects and working together so in  some cases you can even think of them  well as a close-knit Network group of  friends even a kind of family of sorts  and this gives the gives it an identity  okay very good so when when can we  expect the book I'm hoping to finish it  next year next year is a leave year for  me okay and I'm hoping that that after  that shortly after that it will be  complete  one event that will be associated with  with the project as they mentioned that  some of these poets are coming here  they're coming for a conference at Yale  in April called political violence and  militant aesthetics after socialism and  that's actually happening in the Whitney  Humanities Center and is partly  sponsored made possible by the Macmillan  Center so there will be poetry readings  an event at art  face down downtown New Haven with local  artists participating as well as they  yell carry exciting we'll have to look 